,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3818.817254115,"data":"SFT: Satellite imagery is like a big picture of the Earth. It shows us what's happening in different parts of the world. Imagine if you were looking at a big map of the world, but instead of colors, you could see the different shades of blue, green, and brown. That's what satellite imagery looks like. It shows us what's happening in different parts of the world, like the weather, the population, and the land use. It's like a big picture of the Earth, but with colors and information.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3818.817257937,"data":"DPO: Satellite imagery is like a big picture of the Earth. It shows us what's happening in different parts of the world. It's like a map of the world, but it's zoomed in on a small area. It shows us how much rain there is in a certain place, how much pollution there is, and how much sunlight there is. It's like a big picture of the Earth, but it's zoomed in on a small area.\n"}
